lines=['# Joint SPX/VIX refit of the two-speed stress model','', '28 October 2026. The user authorized returning to the two-speed stress model and resuming SPX fitting.', '', '**This first bounded joint fit is not satisfactory overall.** It substantially improves the sampled SPX fit, but loses most of the VIX smile fit. SPX numerical accuracy remains unresolved, so the result is not evidence that the entire two-speed model family cannot fit both markets.', '', '## What was fitted','', 'The model is unchanged:', '', r'$$v_t=f+(\xi(t)-f)[(1-w)R_t+w\{(1-r)A_t^s+rA_t^f\}],$$', '', r'$$A_t^i=\exp(b_iZ_t^i-\tfrac12b_i^2q_i(t)),\qquad dZ_t^i=-a_iZ_t^i\,dt+\sqrt{2a_i}\,dB_t^i.$$', '', 'The two stress innovations remain independent of each other and the old M2 bank/equity driver. The original M2 dynamics, initial state, risk premia, capped readout and positive spike shift remain fixed. This is a restricted joint calibration, not a refit of the seven original M2 readout coefficients.', '', 'All16 variance-curve levels are now free, including the nine intervals invisible to the VIX-only fit. Also free are the floor, both stress sensitivities, both ordered half-lives, the total stress weight and the fast fraction:23parameters. Bounds retain floor volatility5–12%, variance levels between the floor and0.2, sensitivities0–5 and half-lives1–365days. No new factor, correlation, jump, cap modification or expiry-specific rule was introduced.', '', 'The fit includes1294primary SPX quotes at29,57,119,211,302,666,1030days under the agreed market-only cutoff3 membership. All1751eligible SPX quotes, including457diagnostic-wing quotes, are repriced in the timestep check. All217native VIX quotes and all four forwards are retained. Original source splits are metadata; no market observations are held out.', '', 'The objective gives SPX and VIX families equal total weight, equal weight to their respective maturities, and bid–ask-scaled squared interval distances within each maturity. There is no extra VIX-price preservation constraint or new smoothing penalty. The four VIX forwards are equality constraints on the calibration estimator. Quote signs and unavailable IVs are preserved.', '', 'The first stage fits16curve levels and the floor for40SLSQP iterations. The second allows all23parameters for60iterations. Both stop at their iteration limits; their four forward residuals meet the eligibility threshold1e-5. The best eligible training candidate is selected before checking. There is one local staged search, not a global optimization or systematic multistart study.', '', '## Price-fit trade-off','', 'Smaller losses are better. Losses are scaled pricing errors, not monetary P&L or implied-volatility errors.', '', '| Candidate | Training SPX loss | Checking SPX loss | Training VIX loss | Checking VIX loss |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
